<title>HUNGARY: Hungary Jan-July trade gap $1.7 bln vs $2 bln.</title>
<headline>Hungary Jan-July trade gap $1.7 bln vs $2 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's January-July foreign trade deficit fell to $1.7 billion  from $2 billion for the same period a year ago, the Industry and Trade Ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>The ministry said exports totalled $7.3 billion for the period, up 5.2 percent from the same period last year.</p>
<p>Imports for the same period rose 0.1 percent from a year ago, or $10 million, to $9 billion, the ministry said.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom ++ 36 1 347 4040</p>
